The desk merged reports with similar date symptoms into one known ticket.
The original [incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) describes one queued fix,
but the export's live classification separates the shared parser from the
booking-v3 form hint. These are different problems, not duplicate tickets.

## Count reports by cause

<CauseTable ticket={4471} issueNumbers={{ parser: 1, hint: 2 }} />

The table deduplicates overlapping export rows by report ID, then uses tenant
locale, booking form, and channel to classify each report. Intake tags describe
an initial guess, not an established cause.

- **Parser:** the shared parser reads month first for day-first tenants.
  See [#1 - day-first parser](https://github.com/jbabinski/megadev-s01e03/issues/1).
- **Hint:** the booking-v3 form displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, but reads dates in the
  tenant's day-first order. See [#2 - booking-v3 hint](https://github.com/jbabinski/megadev-s01e03/issues/2).

The table footnotes reports the desk read as one-day moves. The export files
them under parser by tenant and channel; that classification alone does not
independently explain every reported symptom.

## Engineering update: closed 5 October

The [course's engineering update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows)
supersedes the queued-fix description in the original export:

- **Parser: fixed.** Engineering reports `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
  Ticket [#1](https://github.com/jbabinski/megadev-s01e03/issues/1) is closed as completed.
- **Hint: won't fix.** The booking-v3 form was retired.
  Ticket [#2](https://github.com/jbabinski/megadev-s01e03/issues/2) is closed as not planned,
  not as a delivered hint fix.

<Callout>
Closed does not always mean fixed. Keep the two causes and their resolutions
separate; retiring a form is not the same outcome as fixing the parser.
</Callout>

## Triage after the update

Match reports by cause and affected context, not subject alone. Check the
tenant locale, form, channel, and current engineering state before merging.
Deduplicate repeated report IDs before counting. Investigate new reports
against the parser fix or form retirement instead of assuming they are
duplicates of this closed incident.

The accepted [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) is preserved
as history. Its subject-only rule and the old incident's queued-fix claim
should not override the computed evidence or the later engineering update.

